      <!-- Career Summary & Research Vision -->
      <section class="content-section" id="career">
        <div class="section-title-wrapper">
          <h2 class="section-title">🧑‍🎓 Career Summary & Research Vision</h2>
        </div>
        <p>
          Abu Kaisar Md Faisal is a Lecturer in Mechanical Engineering at Khwaja Yunus Ali University (KYAU), Bangladesh, and an active researcher at the <strong>Computational Flow Physics & Experimental Aerodynamics (CFPEA) Lab</strong>, Rajshahi University of Engineering & Technology (RUET), under the supervision of Dr. Mahadi Hasan Masud.
        </p>
        <p>
          His research integrates <strong>high-fidelity numerical simulations (CFD)</strong>, <strong>surrogate modeling (RSM & Genetic Algorithms)</strong>, and <strong>subsonic wind tunnel validation</strong> to design next-generation aerodynamic systems. He investigates how nature-inspired surface modifications—such as humpback whale tubercle protuberances, penguin wing kinematics, and corrugated dragonfly cross-sections—can suppress boundary layer separation and postpone stall.
        </p>
        <p>
          He has contributed to 9 peer-reviewed journal publications, 4 book chapters with Elsevier and Springer Nature, and 3 international conference proceedings, with research appearing in top-tier journals including <em>Physics of Fluids</em>, <em>Ocean Engineering</em>, and <em>Journal of Cleaner Production</em>.
        </p>
      </section>

